{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>And he silenced… unto Moses.</b> The meaning is: since an ordinary person has no power to silence a multitude of six hundred thousand, therefore the verse states that he silenced them unto Moses and not by his own decree. For it is known that Moses was a king, as it is written (Deuteronomy 33:5) ״וַיְהִי בִישֻׁרוּן מֶלֶךְ״, and out of awe of him they fell silent to hear what he would say. And he said <b>עָלֹה נַעֲלֶה וְיָרַשְׁנוּ אֹתָהּ</b> — meaning: even according to the words of the spies, we can prevail against it."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:08:31.614352025Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}